    "updated_at": "2025-02-24T02:21:37Z",
    "body": "Thought about it in days.\nYes, it's clear for the current specification.\n\n----\n\nSo change it to a feature request.\nWhen calling `focus( { focusVisible: false } )`, how about setting focus on an element and removing its focusVisible state?\n\n* When the element isn't the focusElement (activeElement), then set focus only and doesn't show focusVisible state. \nIt's same as current behavior.\n* Else, if the element is currently focused, then don't change the focus element and only remove the focusVisible state.\nIt's the new behavoir.",
